From 41d02fb43a5ee6aa70cfe1b7926974fc1a3f0745 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:40:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Reliability gates (off by default): logprob confidence gate
 before the answer; escalate to a stronger model instead of looping

A. MH_CONFIDENCE_GATE=1: when a turn that made or changed files is about to answer, one extra request on the
   same cached prompt asks whether the saved work meets every explicit term of the request; P(yes) is read from
   the first token's logprobs (max_tokens 1). Below MH_CONFIDENCE_MIN (0.6) the agent is sent back once to check
   the request term by term. Once per request; chat-completions endpoints only; never raises.
B. MH_ESCALATE_MODEL=<model>: when the failed-calls or no-progress detector fires, the next MH_ESCALATE_CALLS
   (2) calls of the turn use that model, then the chat's own model again. Once per turn.

agent/reliability.py holds both; tests/test_reliability_gates.py (10 tests). Full suite: 4483 passed.
Live check on llm.meshpool.ai (deepseek-v4.1-flash): P(yes) 0.93 for a correct answer, 0.00 for a wrong one,
1 output token on ~100 prompt tokens.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: <redacted>
